<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria to import rice, potatoes and beans.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria to import rice, potatoes and beans.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deputy agriculture minister Dimo Uzunov said on Tuesday Bulgaria needs to import 15,000 tonnes of beans, 31,000 tonnes of rice and 73,000 tonnes of potatoes.</p>
<p>Bulgaria faces poor harvests this year due to bad weather conditions and lack of funds.</p>
<p>Uzunov did not say whether any import negotiations were under way.</p>
<p>--Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
